[:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The favorite was Kenya’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/114413"} "Janeth Jepkosgei"] " who had won the 2007 World Championships. In the final she led for the first 200 metres before being passed by her teammate, 18-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/114401"} "Pamela Jelimo"] ", who nobody had heard of prior to 2008, but who had won all her Golden League races earlier in 2008. Jelimo was never headed, winning the race quite easily, setting a World Junior Record in the process. Jepkosgei got the silver medal, followed by Morocco’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/88252"} "Hasna Benhassi"] ", the silver medalist in Athina. Mozambique’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/73626"} "Maria Mutola"] " was running in her fifth Olympic 800 final, having won gold in 2000, and briefly challenged at 600 metres but eventually finished fifth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2259"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/114401"} "Pamela Jelimo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KEN.png"}] "KEN"]] [:td {} "2:03.18 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "1:57.31 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:54.87 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2267"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/114413"} "Janeth Jepkosgei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KEN.png"}] "KEN"]] [:td {} "1:59.72 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "1:57.28 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "1:56.07 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class